Subject: [PATCH 1/3] winmm: Add legacy multimedia compatibility and WOW callbacks
Consolidated from as14725836/wine, upgrade/dwproton-11.0-17:
  d6f3093e737238df5eee860a87810141300245a6
  661925a237a16c4667746bb7e9787fc11b119650
  8160abdb31761c904e8ecaefa39f06765952f970
  df3e063cd10d98a007c33312acf4dda684a6be30
  089bbb7d01c6f04655811dfe35cb3bdd9654bfa0
  b0e10c3ae5c59d55cd394fcc7c4e6c37b8bec1b1
Adapted to WinNative-Emu/proton-wine:
  e6a370ff7db61c230df94996f00131e22f9165cf
Preserve the target's unrelated exports and driver implementation. Include
the full WOW multimedia compatibility set: legacy i386 message exports and
the resolver, task cleanup (WOWAppExit), and the WOW32 callback ring
(NotifyCallbackData registers the 16-bit callback data; WOW32DriverCallback
writes callbacks into that ring). WOWAppExit cleans up task-owned MCI devices
and multimedia timers. Existing timer APIs gain regression coverage.
Includes the foreign-thread MCI cleanup correction from df3e063cd10d.
See README.md and ../../docs/wine-function-patch-audit.md for ABI evidence,
selection rationale, limitations, and the distinction between static checks
and runtime validation.
---
